FBInk v1.25.0-543-g886f25f1: fbink_state_dump() passes two arguments for three
format fields (isTolino, SunxiHasFBDamage, SunxiForceRota) on non-Kobo builds,
so the trailing %s (pixelFormat) reads a garbage pointer and `fbink -e`
segfaults on every Kindle. VeraDroid probes fbink with `-e`, so the boot splash
silently disappeared on real devices.

--- a/fbink.c
+++ b/fbink.c
@@
 #else
 	    false,
+	    false,
 	    FORCE_ROTA_NOTSUP,
 #endif
 	    deviceQuirks.isKindleLegacy,
